        "title": "The Transport Layer - TCP State Machine, UDP, QUIC, Ports, Sockets",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "L3 (02) delivers a packet to a *host*. The transport layer (L4) does two more\nthings that L3 cannot: it picks **which process** on that host (via **ports**),\nand — for TCP — it turns the unreliable, unordered, lossy packet service of IP\ninto a **reliable, ordered byte stream**. That is the whole layer: process\nmultiplexing plus optional reliability. UDP gives you the first and skips the\nsecond; TCP gives you both; QUIC reinvents TCP+TLS on top of UDP."
    }
